WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.201
-Chris.
-How are you?

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:04.303
-Thank you so much
for coming on the show, bud.

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.739
It's great to see you.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.509
-Jimmy Fallon, how's it going?

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.711
How -- How's your summer been,
Jimmy?

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:15.214
-[ Laughing ]

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.616
I'm learning.
I'm learning.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.285
I'm always learning, man.
You know I love you, buddy.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.320
-Hey!
Hey!

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.888
I love how they always say
"the one and only."

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:26.058
Like, I know you've been
duped before.

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:28.727
-[ Laughing ]
I know.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:30.296
But I say -- I know.
Well, it just fits.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:34.233
-I know we -- the last time,
we had the fake Chris Rock on,

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.835
but tonight,
it's the one and only.

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:39.038
-It fits.
It fits with your name.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.607
"The one and only."
-Just saying.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.841
-Yeah, I know.
-If you're gonna fake

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.610
being a celebrity,
why would you fake me?

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.178
You know what I mean?
I'd fake being "The Rock,"

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.781
actually, more than fake me,
Chris Rock.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.118
That seems a lot more fun.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:56.155
-We got to Zoom
a couple times together,

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.924
and this is --
it's always interesting.

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:01.961
I don't know when to --
on the ones that we were on,

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:05.398
when to make a joke,
when to come in.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.069
You know, like -- are people
waiting on us to make jokes?

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:13.606
-We had some epic Zooms
this summer.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.643
-Like, crazy ones,
where it's just like --

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:20.046
I was just kind of sitting back,
because like -- wow.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:25.652
Just watching --
-Me, you, Leo, Matt Damon,

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.988
Kevin Hart, Sandler.
-Sandler.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.456
-I remember --
I did ones that, like --

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:35.161
It was, like, me, Kevin Hart,
and Tom Brady.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.831
You know, like --
I don't really know Tom Brady.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.865
-Wow.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.900
-But it was nice
to talk with him.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.335
-Yeah.
-Get acquainted.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.636
-It was crazy.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:47.072
-Like, some epic,
ridiculous zooms.

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:50.243
-Chappelle, I think, was on --
How was...

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.944
-Yes.
-...Camp Chappelle?

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:54.346
'Cause I know Questlove
saw you there.

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:56.216
-Camp Chappelle was great.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:59.252
I think I may go back --
Man, who knows.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.520
I may end up there this weekend.
You never know.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.290
-Right.
-Yeah. Have you been yet?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.093
-No, I do want to go,
'cause, honestly,

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.195
I miss performing
in front of a crowd.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.763
-You gotta go.
You get off your plane,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.967
they test you
for COVID immediately.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.702
-Really?
-And once you get tested,

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:19.838
once your test comes back
negative, you get a wristband.

00:02:19.838 --> 00:02:22.475
And now you can enter
the inner sanctum.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.443
-Yes.
-So, everybody --

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.312
You can look --
everybody's got a wristband.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.382
So no one's got COVID.
-Wow.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.518
-And so you can actually
hang out with people all week.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:34.921
You know,
drink, smoke, whatever.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:38.590
And just have a COVID-free time.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.428
-And what was it like
going in front of an audience?

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.164
-It was kind of a cool.
Remember at the comedy clubs,

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:49.001
I always said, like, the rain
crowd was always the best,

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.370
because they really
wanted to be there?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.538
-Yeah.
-Know what I mean?

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:53.639
-They're happy to be indoors.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.541
-Well, the COVID crowd
is even better.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:03:00.446
Like, the COVID crowd is very
happy that there's a show.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:03.215
-Yeah, they want to be --
They want entertainment.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:04.950
They're like, "Yes!"

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.852
-"Just give us anything!

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:12.858
We are -- we have watched
'Tiger King' far too many times.

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:16.395
Give us anything."
-You said that the pandemic

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:20.966
has been for you like what an
off-season is for an athlete.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.869
What do you mean by that?
-I've just been --

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:27.373
You know what?
I had all this time.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.308
It's like,
"What are you going to do?"

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:32.378
Well, I mean, so I --

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:36.616
I started working out
in a weird, like, obsessive way.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:40.086
In like a kind of Kevin Hart,
Joe Piscopo way.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:44.490
Just been like --
[ Grunting ]

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.526
Working out.
I learned to swim.

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:49.361
I've been swimming a lot.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:52.698
'Cause I couldn't swim forever.
-Oh, I didn't know that.

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.133
-Yeah, I grew up in the hood.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:58.671
It's hard to swim with the water
from a fire hydrant, you know?

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.339
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:03.976
When a fire hydrant
is your ocean.

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.813
-Yeah, exactly.
Just doggy pad-- yeah.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.449
-You can work on a few strokes,
but you know...

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:10.950
-The pressure
pushes you back, yeah.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.386
-It's really hard to really --
yeah.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.421
It's -- yeah, that's how I --
yeah.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.189
It's just hard to -- yeah.

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:19.591
-That's fun the way --
-Swim on 125th Street.

00:04:19.591 --> 00:04:22.395
-I always think of you, Chris,
'cause I feel like you

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:25.898
and Bill Murray always end up
in these places where I go,

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.466
"What is going on?
What --

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:30.603
How did you end up --
Who did you...?"

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.972
And I always think about
it all the time.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.274
You were hanging out

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:37.176
with YouTube star
David Dobrik recently.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.344
That's what
made me think of this.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.012
-Yeah, I like David.
I like David.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.948
-How did you meet --
How do you end up --

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:45.751
How does David Dobrik
and Chris Rock end up together?

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:49.022
-Well, you gotta understand,
my kids are like my focus group

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.689
at this point.
-Yep.

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:54.126
-And if they say somebody's
funny, then they're funny to me.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:55.595
I don't -- You know.
-That's right.

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:59.532
-So, my kids, they've left
Kevin Hart, you know?

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:02.268
And now they're on
David Dobrik, right?

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.736
And I'm watching this stuff.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.871
And they're like,
"He lives in the Valley."

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:09.542
And I'm like, "Well..."
We were in L.A. at the time.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.710
"Yeah, let's go see him.
Let's see what he's doing."

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:15.681
So, I made a couple of calls,
and I talked to him,

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.316
I say, "Is it okay
if I stop by?"

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:18.984
Never met him before,
by the way.

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:20.987
-He's great.
-And he said, "Sure."

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:24.490
So I just -- me and my kids,
we got in the truck,

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.727
we first made a stop
at In-N-Out,

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.528
'cause that's what you do
when you're in L.A.

00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:31.497
Gotta get your In-N-Out.
-You have to.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.967
-And then we went over
to David's house, you know?

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:38.537
And we hung out for, you know,
half a day or whatever.

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:41.106
And now me and David
are like this.

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:45.043
-No, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, I know -- yeah, right.

00:05:45.043 --> 00:05:48.047
-Like this!
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:51.083
You've always been recognizing
great talent in people.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:53.685
Most recently, I think,
Leslie Jones.

00:05:53.685 --> 00:05:58.123
But you once tried to get --
is this true? --

00:05:58.123 --> 00:06:03.896
Cardi B into comedy?
-Well...

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:08.133
Yes, I've been --
When I say recognize talent --

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:11.570
People are so obviously funny,
it's like, yes.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.507
So, I remember I used to try
to get Leslie Jones an agent

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:17.309
for years, and no one
would listen to me.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:20.046
Finally -- of course,
Lorne Michaels is a genius.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:23.750
And he asked me if I knew
any black women for "SNL."

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.118
I said,
"I might have somebody for you."

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:29.121
So, yeah,
I knew Leslie Jones early.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:32.224
I'll say J.B. Smoove premiered
on "The Chris Rock Show."

00:06:32.224 --> 00:06:37.163
-Yeah.
-Hannibal.

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:40.900
I remember pitching
Wendy Williams to HBO

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.437
for a show 20 years ago, and
they didn't want to go for it.

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:46.939
-For a talk show?
-But the latest person --

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:49.908
A talk show, yeah.
They thought I was crazy.

00:06:49.908 --> 00:06:52.011
-Geez.
-Yeah.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.545
-And look at her now.
She's phenomenal.

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:55.281
Of course, Wendy Williams.
-Yeah, look at her now.

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:56.916
God bless her.
-But what happened with Cardi B?

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.851
-She's doing exactly what I knew
she was gonna do.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:01.954
-Yeah.
-Cardi B, I saw, like,

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:04.623
on some YouTube thing
or whatev--

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:07.693
Again, my kids showed me
this Cardi B girl.

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:10.829
And she didn't have
a record out or anything.

00:07:10.829 --> 00:07:12.899
And I was like, "Okay,
we should go show it."

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:14.833
I'm not even gonna say
what network, but --

00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:19.972
So I went -- me, Cardi B,
and her management, you know,

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:22.541
to, like,
kind of get a show going.

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:25.678
And it just never happened.
But I thought she was --

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:28.146
And she told me
about her rap at the time.

00:07:28.146 --> 00:07:29.949
And I was like, "Yeah, yeah,
that's good, good.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.985
Anyway, you're a comedy star."
-Yeah.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.821
-So...
-She is really funny.

00:07:35.821 --> 00:07:38.390
-She is really --
I think Cardi B's

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:43.028
the funniest woman -- or, one of
the funniest people, you know...

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:46.531
-Yeah.
-It's like Chappelle, Cardi.

00:07:46.531 --> 00:07:47.633
You know what I mean?
Like...

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.234
[ Both laugh ]

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:52.671
Like, in the standings
right now, like,

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:55.341
two of the funniest people
in the world.

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:57.109
-Yeah.
-Cardi's right up there.

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.144
She's neck-and-neck
with Bill Burr.

00:07:59.144 --> 00:08:02.448
You know what I mean?
Like, she's good, man.

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:04.950
-Bill Burr.
He's awesome.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:08.487
-Bill puts a little more
writing into it,

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:10.856
but Cardi can hang with anybody.

00:08:10.856 --> 00:08:12.892
-Can you stick around?
I want to talk about "Fargo."

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:14.994
I'm really excited about this.
-Sure.

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.728
-All right, cool.
-For you, I'll do it.

00:08:16.728 --> 00:08:18.698
-More with Chris Rock when we
come back, everybody.

